event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CUgragW4WF298j7VfmRFB6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 9372, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017JTMtKE1wcwDjZrT7SNd2o", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 9672, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017JTMtKE1wcwDjZrT7SNd2o", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 9672, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017JTMtKE1wcwDjZrT7SNd2o", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 9672, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01E9a9g5hLw7iM2M1xEodcya", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 in us-east, us-west and eu-west). Per the platform runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in the deployment history. Note that v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 10272, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01E9a9g5hLw7iM2M1xEodcya", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10272, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01E9a9g5hLw7iM2M1xEodcya", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 11990, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy, and v2.2.9 is older, so v2.3.0 was the right target. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the follow-up items. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nStill to do: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anyone redeploys it. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging, so that is worth checking too.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019wYfWsVPRu9JgBWWgFgHfV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WkKJc5j9VxLVbnZHemFeg7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release is v2.3.1, which is unhealthy. The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0, and it has been healthy before, so the rollback doesn't need change-manager approval. Rolling back to v2.3.0 now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CUgragW4WF298j7VfmRFB6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017JTMtKE1wcwDjZrT7SNd2o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01E9a9g5hLw7iM2M1xEodcya", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 in us-east, us-west and eu-west). Per the platform runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in the deployment history. Note that v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy, and v2.2.9 is older, so v2.3.0 was the right target. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the follow-up items. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nStill to do: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anyone redeploys it. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging, so that is worth checking too.", "type": "text"}]}]}